### Component 2: Leitner Engine & Client Storage (Mobile Client)

We will implement the Leitner Engine on the Flutter client, including entity models, local database queries, progression calculations, due-date check timers, and client-side event bus triggers.

#### [NEW] [domain_events.dart](file:///E:/projects/leitner-learning-platform/mobile-app/lib/core/event_bus/domain_events.dart)
Define client domain events: `CardReviewed`, `CardFinished`, `DueDateOverdueReset`, and `LeitnerProgressReset`.

#### [NEW] [card_progress.dart](file:///E:/projects/leitner-learning-platform/mobile-app/lib/features/flashcards/domain/entities/card_progress.dart)
Represent a card's current box, last review date, next review due date, and sync status.

#### [NEW] [flashcard.dart](file:///E:/projects/leitner-learning-platform/mobile-app/lib/features/flashcards/domain/entities/flashcard.dart)
Represent a card's question, answer, media URLs, and progress.

#### [NEW] [card_progress_model.dart](file:///E:/projects/leitner-learning-platform/mobile-app/lib/features/flashcards/data/models/card_progress_model.dart)
SQLite database serialization/deserialization mapping for progress entries.

#### [NEW] [flashcard_repository.dart](file:///E:/projects/leitner-learning-platform/mobile-app/lib/features/flashcards/domain/repositories/flashcard_repository.dart)
Interface for Leitner Engine database operations:
- `getReviewQueue(String courseId)`: Retrieves Box 1 cards + active due cards from Boxes 2–5.
- `submitReview(String courseId, int cardNumber, bool isCorrect)`: Saves review status, calculates next box/due date, and fires event.
- `resetCardProgress(String courseId, int cardNumber, String reason)`: Returns card to Box 1, resets due date, and fires event.
- `checkForOverdueResets(String courseId)`: Scans for cards whose due dates passed on previous calendar days, resetting them to Box 1 and firing `DueDateOverdueReset` events.
- `syncProgress()`: Pushes unsynced changes to backend and updates local database `is_synced` status.
- `getCourseStatistics(String courseId)`: Collects count of cards per box.

#### [NEW] [flashcard_repository_impl.dart](file:///E:/projects/leitner-learning-platform/mobile-app/lib/features/flashcards/data/repositories/flashcard_repository_impl.dart)
Implement database query execution, spaced repetition progression timing (3, 7, 16, 31 days), and HTTP sync logic.

#### [MODIFY] [injection_container.dart](file:///E:/projects/leitner-learning-platform/mobile-app/lib/injection_container.dart)
Register the new `FlashcardRepository` in the service locator.

#### [NEW] [leitner_engine_test.dart](file:///E:/projects/leitner-learning-platform/mobile-app/test/leitner_engine_test.dart)
Write extensive unit and scenario tests verifying:
- Progression timings (Box 1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4 -> 5 -> Finished) on correct answer.
- Reset to Box 1 on incorrect answer.
- Overdue logic (Rule A) based on calendar days.
- Out-of-order viewing reset (Rule B & Rule C).
- Review queue isolation.
- Sync push updates local `is_synced` flag.

